On Monday 10 January 2011 23:57:27 Robin Lee Powell wrote:
> I was thinking like July or August.  Much nicer around here then,
> IMO.

I have a couple of vaguely scheduled events: I'm planning a trip in March with 
someone I haven't heard from in a couple of weeks, which is making it 
difficult; and I don't know how long my mother's estate will take to probate. 
If the jbonunsla is after the estate finishes probating, I should have enough 
money to pay for the trip; otherwise I won't.

> Oh, a more general question: would people prefer we avoid the
> holiday weekends?  On the one hand, more time; on the other hand,
> more other obligations.

I have no habit of visiting family on holiday weekends, if that's what you 
mean.

> I'd still really like to hear from more people on whether they want
> it to be with a convention.

Depends on the convention and how well we're integrated into it. I liked 
Penguicon, and both times we were easy to find by the other convention-goers. 
A meeting consisting of just Lojbanists would be good too.

